From 716659841014ead06d26ca46667ff18db0be9532 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:32:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/49] B70-V32-03: PLE NVMe n-gram ids hashed on the host
 (B70_PLE_INT8_NVME host path, B70_PLE_HOST_IDS=1)

The NVMe PLE producer needs the step ids on the host; under async scheduling the tokens exist
only on the device, so a sync is inherent. Before: ~50 eager hash ops queued after the previous
step, then a blocking D2H of the [T, heads] ids. Now: one D2H of tokens + n-gram context, the
same arithmetic in numpy (b70_host_ngram_ids; int64 products wrap as torch's do), ids passed to
prepare(host_ids=...). CPU test: numpy == torch eager path, 200 random layouts.
---
